1
00:00:00,250 --> 00:00:02,863
Something's after my mug.

2
00:00:03,013 --> 00:00:05,625
Pip doesn't drink coffee.

3
00:00:05,775 --> 00:00:08,388
Very considerate of him.

4
00:00:08,538 --> 00:00:12,400
You haven't heard what he wants.

5
00:00:15,250 --> 00:00:18,175
Where'd he go?

6
00:00:18,325 --> 00:00:20,331
Keep looking.

7
00:00:20,481 --> 00:00:24,325
I found a mustache.

8
00:00:24,475 --> 00:00:27,400
That's yours, Dad.

9
00:00:30,250 --> 00:00:32,403
Is that his lunch?

10
00:00:32,553 --> 00:00:34,191
It's the moon.

11
00:00:34,341 --> 00:00:38,553
I saw a banana. I must be hungry.

12
00:00:38,703 --> 00:00:42,400
Please leave the sky in one piece.

13
00:00:45,250 --> 00:00:48,432
Did Rose like your cake story?

14
00:00:48,582 --> 00:00:51,250
She laughed at the strawberry.

15
00:00:51,400 --> 00:00:53,553
What's this one called?

16
00:00:53,703 --> 00:00:57,400
I want you to see it first.

17
00:01:00,250 --> 00:01:03,432
How many tickets do you need?

18
00:01:03,582 --> 00:01:04,706
Just one.

19
00:01:04,856 --> 00:01:07,523
For which one of us?

20
00:01:07,673 --> 00:01:12,400
It's a family ticket. You can all squeeze in.

21
00:01:15,250 --> 00:01:19,112
Does he live up there too?

22
00:01:19,262 --> 00:01:21,250
No, down here.

23
00:01:21,400 --> 00:01:24,637
I'll be the moon, then.

24
00:01:24,787 --> 00:01:27,400
Nice job. Great view.

25
00:01:30,250 --> 00:01:33,175
Every great actor takes a bow.

26
00:01:33,325 --> 00:01:36,723
Is his nose supposed to land first?

27
00:01:36,873 --> 00:01:38,852
Only on opening night.

28
00:01:39,002 --> 00:01:42,400
His nose would like a day off.

29
00:01:45,250 --> 00:01:50,973
Little steps, Dad. He's working up to
something.

30
00:01:51,123 --> 00:01:52,649
A jump?

31
00:01:52,799 --> 00:01:54,325
A question.

32
00:01:54,475 --> 00:01:57,400
I know that walk.

33
00:02:00,250 --> 00:02:04,304
Dad, your shoe got here before you.

34
00:02:04,454 --> 00:02:07,943
Did it save me a seat?

35
00:02:08,093 --> 00:02:09,325
Two, actually.

36
00:02:09,475 --> 00:02:12,400
Good. My other foot's coming.

37
00:02:15,250 --> 00:02:17,312
Look at that tail!

38
00:02:17,462 --> 00:02:21,497
His nose is here. His tail's practically
downtown.

39
00:02:21,647 --> 00:02:24,695
Should we send it bus fare?

40
00:02:24,845 --> 00:02:27,400
It knows the way home.

41
00:02:30,250 --> 00:02:33,739
I'm ready whenever the sun is.

42
00:02:33,889 --> 00:02:36,814
It didn't get your schedule.

43
00:02:36,964 --> 00:02:40,454
You can put your foot down.

44
00:02:40,604 --> 00:02:42,400
Oh, thank goodness.

45
00:02:45,250 --> 00:02:49,304
We have a light that stays put.

46
00:02:49,454 --> 00:02:51,814
The little desk lamp?

47
00:02:51,964 --> 00:02:54,325
Does it take direction?

48
00:02:54,475 --> 00:02:57,400
Beautifully. It has one button.

49
00:03:00,250 --> 00:03:03,916
I can see light through it.

50
00:03:04,066 --> 00:03:07,140
Can you see me wink?

51
00:03:07,290 --> 00:03:09,177
Are you winking?

52
00:03:09,327 --> 00:03:12,400
For a whole minute now.

53
00:03:15,250 --> 00:03:19,304
Can I be in charge of something?

54
00:03:19,454 --> 00:03:22,943
You're in charge of the ending.

55
00:03:23,093 --> 00:03:24,889
And the ticket?

56
00:03:25,039 --> 00:03:27,400
Two very important departments.

57
00:03:30,250 --> 00:03:33,916
Who's going to stand in line?

58
00:03:34,066 --> 00:03:37,140
Is it a long line?

59
00:03:37,290 --> 00:03:40,363
Dad, you're the entire line.

60
00:03:40,513 --> 00:03:42,400
Move along, then.

61
00:03:45,250 --> 00:03:48,579
Which side do I sit on?

62
00:03:48,729 --> 00:03:51,519
Can you see the lamp?

63
00:03:51,669 --> 00:03:54,460
Just a bright white screen.

64
00:03:54,610 --> 00:03:57,400
Best seat in the house.

65
00:04:00,250 --> 00:04:03,929
How high is the moon?

66
00:04:04,079 --> 00:04:06,339
A little higher.

67
00:04:06,489 --> 00:04:07,860
Here?

68
00:04:08,010 --> 00:04:12,400
Perfect. I can see both tips.

69
00:04:15,250 --> 00:04:19,117
He's about as big as my thumb.

70
00:04:19,267 --> 00:04:22,058
Big enough to go visiting.

71
00:04:22,208 --> 00:04:25,537
All the way to the moon?

72
00:04:25,687 --> 00:04:27,400
Somebody ought to.

73
00:04:30,250 --> 00:04:35,000
Once there was a mouse who—

74
00:04:35,150 --> 00:04:36,634
Squeak!

75
00:04:36,784 --> 00:04:38,269
Dad.

76
00:04:38,419 --> 00:04:42,400
Oh. Was that your line?

77
00:04:45,250 --> 00:04:48,323
Can I do his voice?

78
00:04:48,473 --> 00:04:51,547
Sure. I'll take the feet.

79
00:04:51,697 --> 00:04:54,177
What about the tail?

80
00:04:54,327 --> 00:04:57,400
It came with the feet.

81
00:05:00,250 --> 00:05:04,105
Bring him a little closer.

82
00:05:04,255 --> 00:05:05,878
This way?

83
00:05:06,028 --> 00:05:08,395
Just a little.

84
00:05:08,545 --> 00:05:12,400
He wants to say hello.

85
00:05:15,250 --> 00:05:19,167
Dad, his ear's getting bigger.

86
00:05:19,317 --> 00:05:21,722
That's some hello.

87
00:05:21,872 --> 00:05:23,333
Bigger.

88
00:05:23,483 --> 00:05:27,400
He's a very good listener.

89
00:05:30,250 --> 00:05:33,175
Wait. Where's the moon?

90
00:05:33,325 --> 00:05:36,250
It was right there.

91
00:05:36,400 --> 00:05:40,024
The mouse ate the moon!

92
00:05:40,174 --> 00:05:42,400
In one bite?

93
00:05:45,250 --> 00:05:48,739
Anything to say for yourself, Pip?

94
00:05:48,889 --> 00:05:50,121
Excuse me.

95
00:05:50,271 --> 00:05:54,325
Was that the moon coming back up?

96
00:05:54,475 --> 00:05:57,400
That was his polite burp.

97
00:06:00,250 --> 00:06:02,863
Did it fall off?

98
00:06:03,013 --> 00:06:05,000
Feel right here.

99
00:06:05,150 --> 00:06:07,138
Still clipped on.

100
00:06:07,288 --> 00:06:12,400
So you can call off the search party.

101
00:06:15,250 --> 00:06:17,617
There's one tip.

102
00:06:17,767 --> 00:06:20,134
And the other?

103
00:06:20,284 --> 00:06:23,395
Back where it belongs.

104
00:06:23,545 --> 00:06:27,400
All right. One moon recovered.

105
00:06:30,250 --> 00:06:33,916
Is he going to burp again?

106
00:06:34,066 --> 00:06:36,547
That wasn't the ending.

107
00:06:36,697 --> 00:06:40,363
Oh. Do you want another try?

108
00:06:40,513 --> 00:06:42,400
In a minute.

109
00:06:45,250 --> 00:06:50,273
What happens if he eats the moon?

110
00:06:50,423 --> 00:06:51,949
Everybody laughs.

111
00:06:52,099 --> 00:06:53,626
And then?

112
00:06:53,776 --> 00:06:57,400
There's nobody left to invite.

113
00:07:00,250 --> 00:07:03,323
Can I borrow the light?

114
00:07:03,473 --> 00:07:05,360
It's all yours.

115
00:07:05,510 --> 00:07:09,177
My hand's right by the screen.

116
00:07:09,327 --> 00:07:12,400
I can count your fingers.

117
00:07:15,250 --> 00:07:19,112
May I shake your enormous hand?

118
00:07:19,262 --> 00:07:21,875
It's the same hand.

119
00:07:22,025 --> 00:07:24,013
My mistake, sir.

120
00:07:24,163 --> 00:07:27,400
You can still shake it.

121
00:07:30,250 --> 00:07:33,175
Your fingers didn't grow at all.

122
00:07:33,325 --> 00:07:36,723
I'd need a sock for each finger.

123
00:07:36,873 --> 00:07:38,379
What did grow?

124
00:07:38,529 --> 00:07:42,400
The shadow. I can see both from here.

125
00:07:45,250 --> 00:07:47,970
I meant closer to the moon.

126
00:07:48,120 --> 00:07:51,280
I thought you meant closer to me.

127
00:07:51,430 --> 00:07:54,590
He got pretty close to his lunch.

128
00:07:54,740 --> 00:07:58,340
Next time I'll point where you can see.

129
00:08:00,250 --> 00:08:03,782
Here's a path for his feet.

130
00:08:03,932 --> 00:08:07,464
Can he turn around on it?

131
00:08:07,614 --> 00:08:08,718
Sure.

132
00:08:08,868 --> 00:08:12,400
Good. It's a long walk backward.

133
00:08:15,250 --> 00:08:18,487
Keep the giant spot too.

134
00:08:18,637 --> 00:08:21,250
Here by the lamp?

135
00:08:21,400 --> 00:08:24,013
We might need it.

136
00:08:24,163 --> 00:08:27,400
That's a suspicious little smile.

137
00:08:30,250 --> 00:08:33,874
Closer to the screen, Dad.

138
00:08:34,024 --> 00:08:36,250
This blue strip?

139
00:08:36,400 --> 00:08:37,926
Right there.

140
00:08:38,076 --> 00:08:42,400
Little feet are back in business.

141
00:08:45,250 --> 00:08:48,579
Now slide him toward the moon.

142
00:08:48,729 --> 00:08:50,981
Still along the screen?

143
00:08:51,131 --> 00:08:53,921
Yes. He wants to visit.

144
00:08:54,071 --> 00:08:57,400
Good. He's had quite enough lunch.

145
00:09:00,250 --> 00:09:02,476
Is Pip nervous?

146
00:09:02,626 --> 00:09:04,851
That's my hand.

147
00:09:05,001 --> 00:09:07,926
You can breathe, Dad.

148
00:09:08,076 --> 00:09:12,400
I was hoping you'd say that.

149
00:09:15,250 --> 00:09:18,211
Greetings, enormous ball of sky!

150
00:09:18,361 --> 00:09:20,750
Do you know him?

151
00:09:20,900 --> 00:09:22,004
Who?

152
00:09:22,154 --> 00:09:27,400
That man who just came out of your mouth.

153
00:09:30,250 --> 00:09:35,161
Can you hear me from there?

154
00:09:35,311 --> 00:09:37,044
Every word.

155
00:09:37,194 --> 00:09:39,722
Even like this?

156
00:09:39,872 --> 00:09:42,400
Especially like that.

157
00:09:45,250 --> 00:09:48,739
Could I move him and talk?

158
00:09:48,889 --> 00:09:50,121
Both jobs?

159
00:09:50,271 --> 00:09:54,889
I know where his feet want to go.

160
00:09:55,039 --> 00:09:57,400
Then you'd better drive.

161
00:10:00,250 --> 00:10:01,690
Got him?

162
00:10:01,840 --> 00:10:03,940
I've got him.

163
00:10:04,090 --> 00:10:07,510
There goes my acting career.

164
00:10:07,660 --> 00:10:12,400
Stay close. Your knees were very good.

165
00:10:15,250 --> 00:10:19,112
How much room do I have?

166
00:10:19,262 --> 00:10:21,250
About a mouse.

167
00:10:21,400 --> 00:10:22,763
Which way?

168
00:10:22,913 --> 00:10:27,400
I'll tell you before you run out.

169
00:10:30,250 --> 00:10:32,863
There goes his nose.

170
00:10:33,013 --> 00:10:35,625
There go his ears.

171
00:10:35,775 --> 00:10:38,388
Does his tail know?

172
00:10:38,538 --> 00:10:42,400
It's always the last to hear.

173
00:10:45,250 --> 00:10:48,916
I can't see where I've gone.

174
00:10:49,066 --> 00:10:51,547
I could take him.

175
00:10:51,697 --> 00:10:54,770
Could you just stay here?

176
00:10:54,920 --> 00:10:57,400
I can do that.

177
00:11:00,250 --> 00:11:03,670
A little to your left.

178
00:11:03,820 --> 00:11:05,260
This left?

179
00:11:05,410 --> 00:11:08,830
Oh! I meant my left.

180
00:11:08,980 --> 00:11:12,400
We brought two of those?

181
00:11:15,250 --> 00:11:18,175
Whose left are we using?

182
00:11:18,325 --> 00:11:20,121
Mine, I thought.

183
00:11:20,271 --> 00:11:23,196
Mine came with these shoes.

184
00:11:23,346 --> 00:11:27,400
Let's pick something that isn't wearing shoes.

185
00:11:30,250 --> 00:11:32,730
Toward the moon, Max.

186
00:11:32,880 --> 00:11:35,953
Can you see me yet?

187
00:11:36,103 --> 00:11:38,584
I've got a nose.

188
00:11:38,734 --> 00:11:42,400
Hang on. The rest is coming.

189
00:11:45,250 --> 00:11:49,105
Any room for that giant?

190
00:11:49,255 --> 00:11:51,622
After the ending.

191
00:11:51,772 --> 00:11:54,139
A curtain call?

192
00:11:54,289 --> 00:11:57,400
A very big bow.

193
00:12:00,250 --> 00:12:05,519
You'll hear this when it's time.

194
00:12:05,669 --> 00:12:07,528
Who's there?

195
00:12:07,678 --> 00:12:09,538
You are.

196
00:12:09,688 --> 00:12:12,400
Then who's knocking?

197
00:12:15,250 --> 00:12:18,947
I thought somebody was at the door.

198
00:12:19,097 --> 00:12:21,765
It was this little knuckle.

199
00:12:21,915 --> 00:12:25,612
What if the moon had a door?

200
00:12:25,762 --> 00:12:27,400
I'd knock first.

201
00:12:30,250 --> 00:12:33,916
What does that sound like now?

202
00:12:34,066 --> 00:12:37,733
Somebody small wants to come in.

203
00:12:37,883 --> 00:12:40,363
What would you say?

204
00:12:40,513 --> 00:12:42,400
Depends who's there.

205
00:12:45,250 --> 00:12:49,112
After I knock, wait for me.

206
00:12:49,262 --> 00:12:51,250
Until you finish?

207
00:12:51,400 --> 00:12:55,262
Sometimes the last bit comes slowly.

208
00:12:55,412 --> 00:12:57,400
We've got time.

209
00:13:00,250 --> 00:13:04,112
Shall we give them an entrance?

210
00:13:04,262 --> 00:13:06,875
I've been practicing mine.

211
00:13:07,025 --> 00:13:09,637
Dad, that's an exit.

212
00:13:09,787 --> 00:13:12,400
I'll practice it backward.

213
00:13:15,250 --> 00:13:19,112
One ticket for the whole family.

214
00:13:19,262 --> 00:13:21,875
Do elbows count extra?

215
00:13:22,025 --> 00:13:24,637
Only the pointy ones.

216
00:13:24,787 --> 00:13:27,400
I'll tuck them in.

217
00:13:30,250 --> 00:13:33,572
Any cheese to declare?

218
00:13:33,722 --> 00:13:36,250
Only my smile.

219
00:13:36,400 --> 00:13:38,928
That's pretty cheesy.

220
00:13:39,078 --> 00:13:42,400
We'll let it through.

221
00:13:45,250 --> 00:13:48,175
May I see your ticket?

222
00:13:48,325 --> 00:13:52,379
All four of us are on it.

223
00:13:52,529 --> 00:13:54,325
Plus my elbows.

224
00:13:54,475 --> 00:13:57,400
I vouched for those elbows.

225
00:14:00,250 --> 00:14:04,778
Once there was a mouse who lived down here.

226
00:14:04,928 --> 00:14:06,497
There he is.

227
00:14:06,647 --> 00:14:10,188
Every night he saw one light upstairs.

228
00:14:10,338 --> 00:14:12,400
That's a long staircase.

229
00:14:15,250 --> 00:14:17,617
Is anybody home?

230
00:14:17,767 --> 00:14:21,622
Who's knocking on the night?

231
00:14:21,772 --> 00:14:24,139
Just a neighbor.

232
00:14:24,289 --> 00:14:27,400
I know that knock.

233
00:14:30,250 --> 00:14:34,925
If you brought crackers, you can go home.

234
00:14:35,075 --> 00:14:36,179
Crackers?

235
00:14:36,329 --> 00:14:38,718
Everyone thinks I'm cheese.

236
00:14:38,868 --> 00:14:42,400
Well, nobody offered me a plate.

237
00:14:45,250 --> 00:14:48,719
I didn't bring any crackers.

238
00:14:48,869 --> 00:14:50,162
Oh?

239
00:14:50,312 --> 00:14:54,451
I came to ask you something.

240
00:14:54,601 --> 00:14:57,400
Take your time, Pip.

241
00:15:00,250 --> 00:15:02,730
Could I come up?

242
00:15:02,880 --> 00:15:05,953
How high can you jump?

243
00:15:06,103 --> 00:15:07,991
About that high.

244
00:15:08,141 --> 00:15:12,400
Ah. We're going to need another idea.

245
00:15:15,250 --> 00:15:18,175
Would you meet me halfway?

246
00:15:18,325 --> 00:15:21,250
You go up a little?

247
00:15:21,400 --> 00:15:24,325
You come down a little.

248
00:15:24,475 --> 00:15:27,400
That sounds like company already.

249
00:15:30,250 --> 00:15:34,330
I've never been down this far.

250
00:15:34,480 --> 00:15:36,580
How's the view?

251
00:15:36,730 --> 00:15:38,830
You have whiskers!

252
00:15:38,980 --> 00:15:42,400
I've had them all day.

253
00:15:45,250 --> 00:15:47,821
Up a little.

254
00:15:47,971 --> 00:15:49,533
There.

255
00:15:49,683 --> 00:15:54,679
I can see daylight between them.

256
00:15:54,829 --> 00:15:57,400
Just a whisker.

257
00:16:00,250 --> 00:16:05,650
Does anybody ever sit with you up there?

258
00:16:05,800 --> 00:16:07,900
People look up.

259
00:16:08,050 --> 00:16:10,810
But do they stay?

260
00:16:10,960 --> 00:16:12,400
Not usually.

261
00:16:15,250 --> 00:16:18,670
Would you stay for dinner?

262
00:16:18,820 --> 00:16:20,260
What's cooking?

263
00:16:20,410 --> 00:16:23,830
I was hoping you knew.

264
00:16:23,980 --> 00:16:27,400
Good thing I came down.

265
00:16:30,250 --> 00:16:34,112
I saved you the quiet seat.

266
00:16:34,262 --> 00:16:36,875
Can we just sit?

267
00:16:37,025 --> 00:16:39,637
That's what it's for.

268
00:16:39,787 --> 00:16:42,400
I like this table.

269
00:16:45,250 --> 00:16:49,171
Is that the end?

270
00:16:49,321 --> 00:16:51,133
Listen.

271
00:16:51,283 --> 00:16:53,329
The end.

272
00:16:53,479 --> 00:16:57,400
Now can I clap?

273
00:17:00,250 --> 00:17:05,273
Dad, we saved a job for you.

274
00:17:05,423 --> 00:17:07,649
The feet again?

275
00:17:07,799 --> 00:17:10,724
Something a bit larger.

276
00:17:10,874 --> 00:17:12,400
May I?

277
00:17:15,250 --> 00:17:18,579
One bow. I'll tell you when.

278
00:17:18,729 --> 00:17:22,058
Closer to the lamp this time?

279
00:17:22,208 --> 00:17:23,921
Yes, on purpose.

280
00:17:24,071 --> 00:17:27,400
I'll give those ears some room.

281
00:17:30,250 --> 00:17:31,776
Excuse me.

282
00:17:31,926 --> 00:17:33,452
About what?

283
00:17:33,602 --> 00:17:37,926
My ears are in your seat.

284
00:17:38,076 --> 00:17:42,400
Just the cheap seats, I hope.

285
00:17:45,250 --> 00:17:47,238
Watch his nose.

286
00:17:47,388 --> 00:17:50,000
I remember the table.

287
00:17:50,150 --> 00:17:53,388
There. He stuck the landing.

288
00:17:53,538 --> 00:17:57,400
And I kept the whole moon.

289
00:18:00,250 --> 00:18:03,739
That's all there was to him?

290
00:18:03,889 --> 00:18:07,379
Just him and a little light.

291
00:18:07,529 --> 00:18:09,325
Ready to close?

292
00:18:09,475 --> 00:18:12,400
He's earned a night off.

293
00:18:15,250 --> 00:18:19,509
Can you get the last little corner?

294
00:18:19,659 --> 00:18:20,953
Got it.

295
00:18:21,103 --> 00:18:24,177
Here's your ticket, Mr. Director.

296
00:18:24,327 --> 00:18:27,400
I'm keeping my first ticket.

297
00:18:30,250 --> 00:18:34,117
Shall I tell Rose about the giant?

298
00:18:34,267 --> 00:18:36,519
Can I tell her?

299
00:18:36,669 --> 00:18:39,998
Please do. Where will you start?

300
00:18:40,148 --> 00:18:42,400
With the little guy.

301
00:18:45,250 --> 00:18:47,611
I know that nose.

302
00:18:47,761 --> 00:18:50,121
May we come in?

303
00:18:50,271 --> 00:18:52,067
Both of you?

304
00:18:52,217 --> 00:18:57,400
As long as those ears fit through the door.

305
00:19:00,250 --> 00:19:03,323
Where should the moon sit?

306
00:19:03,473 --> 00:19:05,953
Here in the middle.

307
00:19:06,103 --> 00:19:09,177
Does it need a plate?

308
00:19:09,327 --> 00:19:12,400
It mostly came to visit.

309
00:19:15,250 --> 00:19:17,502
I liked the burp.

310
00:19:17,652 --> 00:19:19,904
Better than the ending?

311
00:19:20,054 --> 00:19:26,075
I laughed at the burp. I'm still thinking
about the ending.

312
00:19:26,225 --> 00:19:27,400
Me too.

313
00:19:30,250 --> 00:19:34,112
Hey, Pip. Come a little closer.

314
00:19:34,262 --> 00:19:36,250
Closer to what?

315
00:19:36,400 --> 00:19:40,262
To me. I've got good seats.

316
00:19:40,412 --> 00:19:42,400
And excellent elbows.

317
00:19:45,250 --> 00:19:48,929
Coffee for the little gentleman?

318
00:19:49,079 --> 00:19:52,759
He still doesn't drink coffee.

319
00:19:52,909 --> 00:19:55,878
Then what's he having?

320
00:19:56,028 --> 00:19:57,400
Company.
